Recommendation: Merge 1, 2 and 4
Vulnerability Title

Excessive Database Metadata and Security Information Disclosure

Severity

Medium

Description

The database account can enumerate internal database metadata including:

User accounts
Roles
Groups
Permission assignments
Database objects
Table names
Stored procedure names
Authorization structures

The information is exposed through system catalog tables and administrative procedures.

Evidence
select name,suid,uid
from sysusers
select top 20 *
from sysprotects
sp_helprotect
select name
from sysobjects
where type='U'
Impact

An attacker obtaining database access can:

Enumerate privileged accounts
Map authorization structures
Identify sensitive objects
Discover attack paths
Facilitate privilege escalation attempts
Severity

Medium
